#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092992} :activity/id #uuid "eedb9663-ba7e-5ff2-ad61-597482d1636e" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092992 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093402 :tutorial/content "If the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is invertible, then we can find a solution to the system \n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nby \"pre-multiplying\" both sides of the equation by $A^{-1}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ {I}_{2}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the solution of $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ we simply calculate $\\mathbf{x}=A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nFor instance, to find the solution to the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n we first calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, the solution to this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=3$ and $y=2.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "39b17ee8-086a-5282-a414-c88d455b6107" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3049 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "7bdb49ae-e07e-5e55-b869-25f67ee0ac21" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092993}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092993 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092183 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd"} :step/id #uuid "7e787e4f-33b0-514d-ad4f-569e9dfb525d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092994}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092994 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092184 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"} :step/id #uuid "696d1030-ccb5-5376-b23e-62d38e346070" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092998}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092998 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093404 :tutorial/content "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y &=3 \\\\ 6x+3y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nCan we use the matrix method of $\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}$ to find a solution to this system?\n\nThis system can be represented in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo use this matrix method, we need to find $A^{-1}.$ However\n\n$$\n\\det (A) = 2\\cdot 3 - 1\\cdot 6 =0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ is not invertible. So we cannot use the matrix method to find a solution to the system.\n\nIn general, if the coefficient matrix $A$ is not invertible, there is no unique solution. This means that either\n\n- a solution may not exist, or\n\n- there may be infinitely many solutions." :tutorial/id #uuid "e5e2bff7-df5b-5628-92e3-a50ca8dd6be8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3066 :tutorial/title "Systems of Equations Where the Coefficient Matrix is Singular"} :step/id #uuid "ff58cfed-22a0-501b-8983-7edc00d85964"}] :activity/title "Solving 2x2 Systems of Equations Using Inverse Matrices" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186092433}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050944 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092183 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092023 :question/id #uuid "cb7d8dc0-98eb-53d0-9e48-3b1c2d7f6308" :question/math-academy-id "e-4508" :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y &=2 \\\\ 4x+3y &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n![](images/84/843dcd4359e4b61eb9715966fbbe6c26363ab5cfc57c55f94b6a41a73ec7feb1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](images/b9/b9ba240f93ee3ec8c02e9718d62342dca0e0855e24c7b34ed97758a6eb7c46b8.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf74a139-ec79-5146-acec-8db4355df6a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090285} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b491fa-3547-5fba-b7e4-a07ec08d7555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090286} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4fb44c-643c-5621-a968-e5e855c3228d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090287} {:answer/id #uuid "05ce90d3-dd9d-5cc1-90b9-3adb919bde81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090288} {:answer/id #uuid "1961679b-bcc9-512b-85dd-ea7ba1a134ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090289}] :answer-field/id #uuid "db547192-1728-5daf-81fe-bde3526a1a9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24fe26dd-5d5a-5e5d-a810-f538f0a64f2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367953} {:answer/id #uuid "71ec4c9c-d279-5fbb-9214-3724b0723767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367954} {:answer/id #uuid "7918ae0f-27bb-5932-98ae-9536d724c007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367955} {:answer/id #uuid "c91ed029-6221-5342-b4e5-96f1af55d766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367956} {:answer/id #uuid "02454f49-4ca5-5dbb-a530-a7e5183328e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367954} :answer-field/id #uuid "befe57a3-0833-5fca-834d-5958ad1c152f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367952}] :question/id #uuid "a6d30370-c2bc-519b-ba0f-95ca534628ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-31893" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 2x+2y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092885 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b62e1eb-1ec4-5291-ad55-93653f858e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351961} {:answer/id #uuid "bf2382d4-a63b-54b8-9ac9-b2f41261aaf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353209} {:answer/id #uuid "d62c9f51-34cb-5575-a638-2b65d740feb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353421} {:answer/id #uuid "f21a642e-d30e-54ad-a51c-506a5a378af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353678} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cae15e-a38b-5ccf-be4f-88d2a4973c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353678} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc92412e-c38d-5d25-9549-1444416864f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354140}] :question/id #uuid "c79bea22-6c3f-5522-b32f-6f5b851abe6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-8858" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y &=0 \\\\ 3x-6y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-6)-1\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8a2b0d-d5b3-5494-a8d5-71ccb1bd416a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234593} :answer-field/id #uuid "67b39520-9797-501e-b4fa-f5114ee8090d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b5b2e4-6df0-5c69-b3ce-2762ea4544ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234567} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de6d6a5-daf3-537a-94ab-8241aceddfcb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a90358fb-6302-5266-94d3-c5c04cd00164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234804} :answer-field/id #uuid "b64d1ae8-169d-508d-b88c-817a9ce74bef" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235196}] :question/id #uuid "211421e3-130a-58f3-b6bd-e1f1632e4ff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-138788" :question/problem "The solution of the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+1 &=0 \\\\ 4x+3y-3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ngives the point where the highways meet. This solution can be written in matrix form as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$a\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,b\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,c\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the solution to this system as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ed7825e-346d-5a22-8ed8-59e83678839e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235895} {:answer/id #uuid "3f5e0f07-9e55-5437-8a9f-de7f29f88968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236220} {:answer/id #uuid "81562466-cc96-52f4-a684-36eebfe55435" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236623} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1eec43-5163-52ae-8860-4c008a4b0cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236698} {:answer/id #uuid "d2543379-d127-586c-a68f-81316a7711b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236623} :answer-field/id #uuid "7297e027-56e3-5659-87cd-c6423edce84a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237591}] :question/id #uuid "25d74c84-9d1d-5f1c-8223-f549d1370a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-102705" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y &=1 \\\\ 2x-3y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "064de0c7-096b-5389-8080-9e2ae4764534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250605} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8d8a83-b90f-5180-90d6-a020b14121fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251073} {:answer/id #uuid "9b08396c-9b9b-50dc-a08e-c834744fe172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251888} {:answer/id #uuid "d5eb9222-6c0e-556f-b560-f04038c06a2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252447} {:answer/id #uuid "f1422872-4bb2-5409-903a-825ff487dfde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250605} :answer-field/id #uuid "c19d993e-cabe-5e7a-9e34-3aaa832bda0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253139}] :question/id #uuid "9b922ce0-59e6-5533-889a-0b37907617d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-11981" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=4 \\\\ 2x-y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a999a1bb-7ac8-55d2-8393-2961fe8f6692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255168} {:answer/id #uuid "bad09301-d962-5451-8ac9-40479b90b545" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255333} {: