/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x &=6 \\\\ -3x+4y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $4$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f58a8f10-a7dd-5ec5-91a6-dd16cf7e0d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298598} :answer-field/id #uuid "35030cdb-2e5f-5155-a88b-053c6761376c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b01439bb-9a4d-575d-95e6-87ffb201b5cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{