atrix}46 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390724} :answer-field/id #uuid "94a86967-5a41-5f2d-8c19-38b625daba3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390719}] :question/id #uuid "34c426c5-7657-5020-93fd-26e20c441212" :question/math-academy-id "q-32139" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+6y &=46 \\\\ 8x+y &=-23\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}46 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 8}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}46 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f5b8c41-9275-5085-abef-6a1812aa469f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394788} {:answer/id #uuid "ba181d58-8ebc-580b-bb59-d040b7302269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394789} {:answer/id #uuid "c10a9d61-198c-505f-b96f-83ca77a5a247" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394790} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd23087-1a21-5756-9a57-94c2eb1f694a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394791} {:answer/id #uuid "a28c94e5-2455-5339-81d6-ba859dc3ddf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394790} :answer-field/id #uuid "97cd5c37-7a5a-599e-b258-49eb4d18806c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394787}] :question/id #uuid "ba637199-2f92-58f3-86a2-b0752019d746" :question/math-academy-id "q-8856" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8y &=6 \\\\ -5x+6y &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 8}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092184 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092024 :question/id #uuid "422d31ad-8caa-5ce2-a0e0-c905fcc2640d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4509" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y &=5 \\\\ 6y-5x &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y &=5 \\\\ -5x+6y &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/24/240a1d2f7f93ec808127c9fa1791a77a43fcd7c0c84505540acc81c8b9fbc6e1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](images/78/7850cbafc78f2cf2ce14ae7111064bf2f5a029f4d1b97b6d5ebfc09e7126f44e.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020a2da6-4a5e-575f-ad8f-819547ac3b1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253684} {:answer/id #uuid "9de31456-b053-5715-9a1d-050bb9def06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255059} {:answer/id #uuid "dc802c56-6836-5a13-9d31-fe28e0f393f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255623} {:answer/id #uuid "ebeb34a0-9cad-53b4-b6fd-e33d677f4d34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255734} {:answer/id #uuid "ecc5df92-4ed6-5143-9a68-44061677c730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255738} :answer-field/id #uuid "13b2d081-4962-5f3a-9d01-34302e0cf9f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255951}] :question/id #uuid "ef69c0bd-1e6b-5aa5-8b52-0d9fec08f2b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-12286" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8y &=6 \\\\ -5x &=7-6y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8y &=6 \\\\ -5x+6y &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 8}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bccd7e22-9d2f-55d5-a585-963c2c52e8cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091505} {:answer/id #uuid "04d7a9f7-35c9-5204-a09d-ea360946c5af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091506} {:answer/id #uuid "393a819a-e9b9-5ced-86ec-c7f3f71d69a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091507} {:answer/id #uuid "552c169a-0af2-5304-8ad3-715fa39d203b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091508} {:answer/id #uuid "78071ddb-84be-5063-8e44-a7a8d21faf35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091509}] :answer-field/id #uuid "60ebc66e-bfc3-563f-a5f0-6e3cfbfd3101" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae4964c-f640-51d6-b9c7-f318fd111484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394794} {:answer/id #uuid "17c85b88-207b-522e-a8c6-8f0876a467b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394795} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2499d2-9266-5a26-a0ba-05f6dec3dc83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394796} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d702b1-ea00-5873-b240-8fda112f30b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394797} {:answer/id #uuid "54dc7049-9dbc-5720-9a0e-cef337a14f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394795} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c09813-9278-5368-bde8-427b6b2c6b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394793}] :question/id #uuid "a7ea58d8-c912-5e16-b0bd-a3c96b9a8c0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8857" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x &=5y \\\\ x &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y &=0 \\\\ x &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37503db8-10d7-5583-8f30-374405d5c1fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236171} {:answer/id #uuid "4461e345-3733-5f04-8b2d-ba7bcab3ab70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236258} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca5d4f4-cb39-51c0-989f-7439bc2613f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236501} {:answer/id #uuid "825b8a80-c42c-526f-8704-24d7b15a4dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236631} {:answer/id #uuid "ee57336e-c7c8-555f-8bf6-a84746d0aacb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236258} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe30c037-d401-593e-a43e-6b8a2fcfc035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237773}] :question/id #uuid "9876e0e7-b1e4-559d-b97c-350c8c6823a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-102802" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y &=4 \\\\ 6 &=5x\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y &=4 \\\\ 5x &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237951 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7beab9a8-f3e4-5887-ad6d-af714014f1bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236591} {:answer/id #uuid "84f426dd-988f-5643-a988-220caa26f7a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236643} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee9efea-1ede-57bd-aec3-223261944b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236809} {:answer/id #uuid "aefc5a15-ca4a-515d-a407-869e5ced6763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236933} {:answer/id #uuid "d314a2ef-8484-5c72-a562-073ea1176602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236933} :answer-field/id #uuid "9856937d-1b93-595b-b8fd-c398031474db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237640}] :question/id #uuid "9a9bf5d9-a105-5273-92d8-121826d30910" :question/math-academy-id "q-102806" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5 &=2x-3y \\\\ 4x &=y-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y &=5 \\\\ 4x-y &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237952 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47f76438-6efc-5154-acf2-f6221ba718ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236280} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9a3a70-ee22-53c6-95ac-a12143b1c2c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236424} {:answer/id #uuid "96729604-fadb-5569-aa87-61777a5842be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236771} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5d3eee-3c13-550d-bfe1-19982b6b6b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237020} {:answer/id #uuid "e80f65f0-a584-5cc5-9b86-6e7afa185455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236280} :answer-field/id #uuid "82a38cc5-62a7-5b61-a58b-db932ec1135d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237613}] :question/id #uuid "8f4997ea-9df4-5b85-a287-2f793d51b1ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-102807" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y &=x+3 \\\\ 7-y &=-x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y &=3 \\\\ x-y &=-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dc29ab4-d8ac-5d3d-979b-9f7f98f139d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236107} {:answer/id #uuid "3de44d48-7c55-5446-89cc-29fd5806f50b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236202} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e5c08a-cb31-58b8-b1f4-396df518bf90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236877} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4ec5f6-1181-5431-9305-03d19df17f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236903} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a76ae9-5747-59ff-a6cf-cd7f572a7402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237348} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e11cc4-ab12-593a-b925-941a0b313fdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237452}] :question/id #uuid "af582baa-848b-5255-869a-b91da71ab3e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-102808" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3 &=y \\\\ 3y &=4x+2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=3 \\\\ -4x+3y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65244d9b-e076-530c-a369-4480f47d9556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236459} {:answer/id #uuid "771d3b5c-5ed2-5f37-bd7a-fbfa57df0d52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236566} {:answer/id #uuid "863438cb-8b5e-556d-b853-0da07e2effb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236652} {:answer/id #uuid "868772fc-96c1-56f7-83c3-16a475c414d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236654} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a74150-e44f-5676-97b9-fe72216cdb78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237060} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb07b2ee-24d6-5edd-9fd3-03d48f69b538" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237679}] :question/id #uuid "67ac7207-89ed-556a-b760-e125b88ef308" :question/math-academy-id "q-102809" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x &=1-3y \\\\ 3-4y &=2x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+3y &=1 \\\\ -2x-4y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd5a3c7-d4ea-5555-a387-b04cd2aee012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290751} :answer-field/id #uuid "033694dc-bdfd-5cb2-8efe-ed26421337c9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a8cf0f4-97ea-5779-96de-841428f9ef6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290950} :answer-field/id #uuid "51679d72-6f51-5169-bafc-51ef247f515a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291987} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a2f8c27-efae-567c-bd1a-986f17fcbaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290942} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa98698-b951-50c7-9fcc-b0135cc19a3c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292183}] :question/id #uuid "dbf400af-4fb2-5200-ac54-d2206eb77cb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275763" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y &=1-3x \\\\ x-2 &=-4y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+3y &=1 \\\\ x+4y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd0e2d42-082f-5cbb-b6a8-8d4c0a8451c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298499} :answer-field/id #uuid "013f34b5-20a7-5b3b-9374-6d9d207b9f68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db1d3eb3-9f1e-5f1f-9e29-0ad502292118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298494} :answer-field/id #uuid "72653426-d046-5142-afe9-2eb9cb8e4d19" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb6772ed-bf5c-5100-8200-292ea057d9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298435} :answer-field/id #uuid "f93dc586-43a3-5c3c-88dc-3a1741391d66" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299480}] :question/id #uuid "23128eb9-b5db-5f2f-87a2-462e292d0a60" :question/math-academy-id "q-320810" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x &=y+5 \\\\ x-2 &=-3y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-y &=5 \\\\ x+3y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f457c67a-a649-5300-b733-a6a3d7293588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298590} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eaa4cb5-a40c-56aa-ba65-4658611d179b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc969f3-ec35-513b-a6e8-a774ed0952ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297680} :answer-field/id #uuid "799c0051-ae72-56e8-b9c3-146782b5519a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27d6a72c-1dff-577e-849f-900fd3e85f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297721} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6fb8ef6-11b5-56f8-87c7-44fdda3a1f97" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299307}] :question/id #uuid "963a7f3f-2112-5c95-85ab-958b0db31a33" :question/math-academy-id "q-320811" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y &=7-3x \\\\ x+1 &=-2y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=7 \\\\ x+2y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf6e471d-837e-5baf-91dc-1a3582938b55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298394} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c55ffc-0294-561c-a0f7-2a8e87521060" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020e0f0d-d42c-5b5c-8257-252945685d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297568} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d6aa461-a89a-5912-ae30-46f922ab5b44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da762bc-0470-5a53-8566-0408a5927eb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297617} :answer-field/id #uuid "c93cc016-8b20-516c-af83-95e5abf8b571" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299311}] :question/id #uuid "4fd1af2b-5abb-5719-b412-392f65801ff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320836" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+8 &=0 \\\\ x &=7+3y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $7$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+0y &=-8 \\\\ x-3y &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862d1024-b1ee-5d1b-bccd-fe3564ba0538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298132} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b9900e-2d14-5ff7-8f9b-3dc202a50204" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359923bb-41ad-5a22-8110-231c9af62b6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297766} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed86c5f-7a2e-5792-a0c7-774b7f6dc479" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4093295-e6fc-503d-b1c7-c5949de5c759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298587} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c89783-6eef-5c80-81bf-8abaab3d9452" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299254}] :question/id #uuid "47e2d599-891b-5344-82a3-b9ce814d6215" :question/math-academy-id "q-320842" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y-2x &=5 \\\\ x &=-1-4y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y &=5 \\\\ x+4y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e974c234-2745-5a8a-8b60-ace815e198d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298544} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d594158-9b0d-5f6b-9519-9a1687aa57ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "657f2568-783a-5703-b3fd-c4acec9e64db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297985} :answer-field/id #uuid "923b66ba-005e-5664-80de-a084dc03c9a4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ee4537-cdc6-5cd3-824d-cb987fd4527a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297710} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9ca3c4-c50d-556e-8b08-de663407ce6e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299435}] :question/id #uuid "9e717507-c51a-5c1c-8601-5f1355a3dc79" :question/math-academy-id "q-320847" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 4x &=6-y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $6$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 4x+y &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78cbd9bf-4f06-525b-b262-be3ccf63e9d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300556} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f619b9c-7b20-57dd-adc7-eee213d04645" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301276} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f1a2fb5-d659-5dd6-b788-1e6a9a3df8b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300591} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb2dd88-fad5-5b51-a6f9-5b3964b1b5cf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301434} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "258ab35f-2351-57e5-9b0d-3970eb64953a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300140} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0108aa8-a14a-5cb4-a695-f5eb2e617568" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301805}] :question/id #uuid "51eb37cd-4f75-568b-a384-cdd97a21011c" :question/math-academy-id "q-321437" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x &=8 \\\\ 4y &=5+3x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $5$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $8$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y &=8 \\\\ -3x+4y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3\\text{ } & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98a71847-a5b7-5739-aa80-28539a759d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300729} :answer-field/id #uuid "3861729e-b196-5570-b193-dbaeb56de027" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301408} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dd886a1-31bf-549f-96c2-5114acdefbe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300680} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5af1b0-01b1-50a9-b376-332b6a4edc97" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "651cbbf1-faee-586c-b73e-a7387785ccea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300473} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f06275f-496a-5016-8903-60a2850e54d1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301682}] :question/id #uuid "2cc52558-5774-5127-8008-8b3f9f98aa60" :question/math-academy-id "q-321438" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7y &=-14 \\\\ 2y &=5x+9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $2$ | $-7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-14$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ | $-7$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-14$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+7y &=-14 \\\\ -5x+2y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 2-(-5)\\cdot 7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4fd9d8f-0d00-565a-a456-ec2798104d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300793} :answer-field/id #uuid "31c709b5-024b-51f8-bf73-37eedafd431d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301384} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcf36103-abdd-5cec-bc1a-ba2ff2189144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300906} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f80c196-998b-5e70-9ad3-f40ba465145e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301624} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2cdd95d-91f0-5e73-a548-7ab53821cd95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300854} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a73ca2-d878-56a6-8974-77f2cd9c8238" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301911}] :question/id #uuid "652b355c-c82f-51a3-ab10-8d285623bc25" :question/math-academy-id "q-321439" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x &=3+y \\\\ 5y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $10$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x-y &=3 \\\\ 0x+5y &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03087a9c-7c81-54df-8865-721b36cca8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339150} {:answer/id #uuid "46131c51-26ce-5ae9-bbec-cd76141b268d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339751} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1dacb8-dd5f-529b-a0ea-e1deea46ddbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340091} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8da1b5-c398-579a-aea4-b89e242441c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340270} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fb3893-e722-5a06-a2cf-16fddab1d09d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339751} :answer-field/id #uuid "217eb4c8-abdc-5a9d-9700-26248de988b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341441}] :question/id #uuid "ef160bb4-443b-58b5-915b-9dfda073ef96" :question/math-academy-id "q-72729" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3y \\\\ 2x &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=0 \\\\ 2x &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cae29bf-6657-5948-b4ac-de9d15a83b80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339243} {:answer/id #uuid "1c79ef91-d60f-5461-9182-a09de75ab44e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339373} {:answer/id #uuid "50658568-e9ab-5946-9ac1-0eb64885c225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339861} {:answer/id #uuid "7a038809-9690-59a5-9f4d-8538600ea5bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340216} {:answer/id #uuid "af86119f-4c68-5d25-8752-90c8805840da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340730} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ce73d2-08ab-546f-9ccf-5116afbbd6e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341484}] :question/id #uuid "ae55f4eb-c009-586b-a5eb-f77f0f124cd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72733" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x &=y+1 \\\\ x-y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=1 \\\\ x-y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341853 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a855b3fc-a58c-5d42-a023-aa1cf84fddf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340656} {:answer/id #uuid "b0524785-8288-5abb-802a-012c402c2c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340735} {:answer/id #uuid "c879817f-f47b-5f8c-bd26-909387da2146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340904} {:answer/id #uuid "cd44ee7c-1bb6-5ae0-982d-0157107836dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340948} {:answer/id #uuid "f3324b52-7891-5d54-8104-c33959c84d71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340656} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a776a82-f7c0-52f5-ae5f-436886fab53b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341564}] :question/id #uuid "cc0bf99b-722a-5c69-a1c9-0059727d8fb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-72738" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x &=3y \\\\ y &=-x+1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x-3y &=0 \\\\ x+y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot 1-(-3)\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "795f98a0-cfeb-5e53-9ca4-a39e59752b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367944} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ab6d21-d5ac-5e81-b0b4-ae407584dcfd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c9f43a2-c733-5f0d-bf7d-1d791c0c1338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367946} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbfa6506-27b9-5c30-abe6-f50d7f5d0199" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "157efe8e-971d-5726-84b4-718316ef3184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367948} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f509bb7-1eba-5227-8840-6f3afededcc3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367947}] :question/id #uuid "4290f953-e9cc-53d8-aaec-0e2030ce4110" :question/math-academy-id "q-275760" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+2x &=3 \\\\ x-2y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=3 \\\\ x-2y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-2)-1\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-7)}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc295251-8992-58af-99ad-555c55679954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386050} {:answer/id #uuid "fa3e33dc-c2fa-5ce8-a74b-cafe4387cbba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386051} {:answer/id #uuid "afb508cc-f7c7-553c-b844-811d03f18621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386052} {:answer/id #uuid "38618689-5610-50ab-b2fe-e981dfe08e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386053} {:answer/id #uuid "e35c6576-aa93-5aa2-bc00-3b5fc1b8c2d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386053} :answer-field/id #uuid "a482c228-62c7-528d-a980-052fac0d225f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386049}] :question/id #uuid "0f36e193-cfb7-556d-862d-7ca0f147ebca" :question/math-academy-id "q-102799" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y &=-x \\\\ 2y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=0 \\\\ 2y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c24857-06a2-5e0b-85d2-5f2b717c9839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393217} {:answer/id #uuid "54b091df-4df8-574b-ab7b-0a3fde77dee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393218} {:answer/id #uuid "30420fca-ad93-57fd-ba3b-06ad555ade16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393219} {:answer/id #uuid "e0dddfb6-deca-5831-988a-cc662b273194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393220} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2b60cb-753e-5c81-be84-11c5779434a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393219} :answer-field/id #uuid "b977679f-6256-57c2-8887-0c386f7a473b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393216}] :question/id #uuid "cf30e2dd-fc54-551b-b230-ad61e11fe0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-72726" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y &=4 \\\\ x &=-2y-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y &=4 \\\\ x+2y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :topic/math-academy-id 934 :topic/title "Solving 2x2 Systems of Equations Using Inverse Matrices"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167860} :activity/id #uuid "0a53a252-6ac4-561a-b529-a6d8a0a14ceb" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167860 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168023 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll study phase portraits of linear systems\n![](images/6f/6f6a92e2b8fb89f833268a5526876cb3af5215db0193a2aaaad8aac5790752ea.svg)\nwhere the $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A$ has a *repeated* real eigenvalue $\\lambda$ (algebraic multiplicity $2$).\n\nIf $A$ has *two independent eigenvectors*, then $A$ is the scalar matrix\n![](images/69/69199c6f84ebe1f9587b9207a3f1fc42c909fc9a1e43041e11fcab9ce881e5d1.svg)\nIn this case, every direction through the origin behaves like an eigenvector direction, and trajectories are straight lines:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{\\lambda t} \\mathbf{v}, \\qquad \\mathbf{v} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2.\n$$\n\nSo the phase portrait is a **star node**:\n\n- If $\\lambda>0,$ trajectories move *away* from the origin and we have an **unstable star node**.\n\n- If $\\lambda<0,$ trajectories move *toward* the origin and we have a **stable star node**.\n\nLet's see an example." :tutorial/id #uuid "8fe5f0d1-38d4-5cd2-98f8-8935d82677de" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14569 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b7f1536f-3909-5575-8eee-90d0181e7613" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167861}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167861 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168005 :tutorial/content "Let's sketch the phase portrait of the following linear system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in matrix form, we have\n![](images/f5/f58fb57caaba8c5f6a110c72565c24803ac233f41b8eb2db0c5221bcf12d7fe2.svg)\nwhere ![](images/65/65298928a44147868c82da753a731e35c3aa0ad5e4b3400819d9d9f16f546a34.svg)\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are $\\lambda_1=\\lambda_2=2$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ![](images/69/694a89326f61bbbba7e91db5dcb607a74f99881ce16059450dbe1bbac7ee797e.svg)\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n![](images/ab/abd4dbe3156abbcd645e670fb893f93cc8765cba4b1da9bde11075e211f1eeaa.svg)\n\nNotice that for each vector ![](images/9d/9df6cb20bf3163f53850730242138ec62412ccc8af23098130d71228cac4b82a.svg) we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n![](images/71/7166c456c7912bf31d4ff2d98f4e4206537f8d01aca086fdba3c15b394db4b81.svg)\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector ![](images/23/23074d10911b113811cc92bdc88a61a6758dbd8772c21425159c5e95d30b1075.svg)\n\nSince $e^{2t} \\to \\infty$ as $t \\to \\infty,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t \\to \\infty,$ so the origin is an unstable node.\n\nThe phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/b3/b32b5666c0138f5c17ff1622cef9bca6fb019375f6748b6422c11a547cfad282.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "ae2e5f22-ed77-5781-b5af-ab6ead3ca6d6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14467 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example of a Star Node"} :step/id #uuid "b1d8e327-701e-5016-9351-b19e915b0311" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167862}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167862 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "371d99ed-a060-51da-8f0f-7b38a0267bb7"} :step/id #uuid "470270ef-3713-5eab-bed1-4ac8b8cff293" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167863}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167863 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168024 :tutorial/content "Recall that in this topic, we're studying phase portraits of linear systems\n![](images/28/28d8900ae13325f715af9679fdeab6f26645e322ea0df016618826a5b3dee328.svg)\nwhere the $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A$ has a *repeated* real eigenvalue $\\lambda$ (algebraic multiplicity $2$).\n\nIf $A$ has *only one eigenvector* $\\mathbf{v},$ and if $\\mathbf{w}$ is a generalized eigenvector satisfying\n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nthen the general solution takes the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=c_1 e^{\\lambda t}\\mathbf{v}+c_2 e^{\\lambda t}\\bigl(t\\,\\mathbf{v}+\\mathbf{w}\\bigr).\n$$\n\nHere, the eigenvector line (the line through the origin parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$) is still a straight-line solution, but other trajectories are *curved* and become tangent to that eigenvector line.\n\nIn cases like this, the phase portrait is a **degenerate node**:\n\n- If $\\lambda>0,$ trajectories move *away* from the origin and we have an **unstable degenerate node**.\n\n- If $\\lambda<0,$ trajectories move *toward* the origin and we have a **stable degenerate node**.\n\nLet's see an example." :tutorial/id #uuid "f7b031de-59cf-53fe-be90-ac3711677246" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14570 :tutorial/title "Systems With Repeated Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "75bd8867-e725-5442-988b-67f110d201f4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167864}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167864 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168006 :tutorial/content "Consider the following system of linear differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe eigenvector corresponding to the only eigenvalue of the system's matrix $A$ is ![](images/23/23616d197363a3fd8ad4689a0b1e547c7b1044e0929cfd96add65a26e940731f.svg) The vector ![](images/3e/3e434cc0b5ca5d288695abb58500e8f4ca6be0c0cf2ecb5200d03f5fbcf522c2.svg) is such that $(A - \\lambda I)\\mathbf{w}= \\mathbf{v}.$ \n\nLet's sketch the phase portrait of the system.\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda=1$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $\\mathbf{v},$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = c_1\\mathbf{v} e^{\\lambda t}  + c_2 (\\mathbf{v}  te^{\\lambda t}  +  \\mathbf{w}e^{\\lambda t} \\, ),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{w}$ is a solution to the equation $(A - \\lambda I)\\mathbf{w}= \\mathbf{v}.$\n\nIn our case, \n![](images/0f/0f7c56980abff1ad84ca69aa98730bca2988cf5430f181f69d191f1e3c28eff0.svg) \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n![](images/c9/c9d65d3792c7cced40b86834fbd66769daa714ed58ffcde025cb956763c2c670.svg)\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since $e^{t} \\to \\infty$ as $t \\to \\infty,$ these solutions move toward infinity in the phase plane as $t \\to \\infty.$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/98/98fc60d566b520f3d943e42ee8f4e07aa0bdd33b53fbb04981c2e8f4001210fd.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n![](images/61/6170eec4537e26afef2a794426b4f5231b0f4366c21b8860c332f1ec7573b96a.svg)\nWhen $c_2=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t{e}^{t} \\\\ y={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $1.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.30$ | $0$ | $3.98$ |\n| $y$ | $0.61$ | $1$ | $3.32$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/4f/4fbc1650377d580d7129701d745dc8cad89d2d1d061b8f6dca8127f0ce062dc8.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/49/499391b5bc015bd96bbe85d72e3937e87a5e89081951aaad0a752582cb87f15f.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "bfa66c2a-6bb2-552c-b495-e33f1eabed8c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14468 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example for a System With Repeated Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "459bdc90-2dce-52cb-8f50-0ae602e390e4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167865}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167865 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2c335ee-467a-5114-a7d9-4c2692562d9e"} :step/id #uuid "4664ec49-c2f9-5bce-aa8d-00c4ee9589e6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167866}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167866 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7aa8246d-6476-5574-a9d2-6133bcd169f7"} :step/id #uuid "eb9d67cc-acaf-5e2e-a509-7e2eb99610dd"}] :activity/title "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Repeated Eigenvalues" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167011} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478476} :activity/id #uuid "cacf7310-3c00-5589-9153-aa9a4d046b77" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478476 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167214 :question/id #uuid "cb42e4f6-9c82-5ae7-9fb2-860a5f0fb548"} :step/id #uuid "4a094494-860c-5096-883d-aa966a9b908d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478490}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478488 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478412 :question/id #uuid "6a4095b6-ac86-5129-b614-5959c7d2c664"} :step/id #uuid "b69b8d43-1d59-555c-896c-7caa0cb68dcd"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478490 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478430 :question/id #uuid "a814509c-4749-52dd-b5dc-eeb409609ce5"} :step/id #uuid "be046998-fcd4-5bf6-9080-bdee8bd453b5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478488}}] :activity/title "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Repeated Eigenvalues" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477732} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551449} :activity/id #uuid "d69decd4-cccc-532c-95d7-0674e48dd450" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551407 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551313 :question/id #uuid "97e18a22-6fdc-5ccf-b5b0-b0a200f3d5b5"} :step/id #uuid "61cf691b-d2b0-5082-860e-8f5caf14e159"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551441 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551331 :question/id #uuid "bff2c616-f045-5186-8916-8acfc055fce7"} :step/id #uuid "b2608a3b-a978-5a1c-83d8-9303ec15fa5d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551407}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551449 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478412 :question/id #uuid "6a4095b6-ac86-5129-b614-5959c7d2c664"} :step/id #uuid "cb7582e5-176f-5a5d-bbfa-e84dc4e140e7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551441}}] :activity/title "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Repeated Eigenvalues" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550362}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050967 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166919 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166545 :question/id #uuid "a38dad3a-1afd-5e97-9046-87e413574865" :question/math-academy-id "e-21642" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-8x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-8y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSketch the phase portrait of the linear system above." :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n![](images/73/737c96109e65d59f4df2c2fa574737fe604483fe4ccc9772a3d2bf22ee32e55a.svg)\nwhere ![](images/22/22dbda7d3b169206071e5af49fd1fe1af28d86ef1e0a8b37d58eacb62b44c1d2.svg)\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are $\\lambda_1=\\lambda_2=-8$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ![](images/5b/5bd691bbaa9542184d90e55aeb16f4dfcd3d22d092b4652e8bddba7bf0b926aa.svg)\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n![](images/8b/8b25789fb45234e4299e4b5ce3371c1afafc181c64f9802d212ae7cbefc0970f.svg)\n\nNotice that for each vector ![](images/67/674212f0d815e0588faaf276bd797e9822ac5659e5d4b15a7635d7f1327d5dc5.svg) we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n![](images/d4/d4c31285e6f31a229bc6fc5cbe2d78e2bf50f73bb6305d91687c5dcc31c3885a.svg)\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector ![](images/26/268764bbe776b03647daac7fc77e8ed24107e1bb0cf16d955f7a845a12c65755.svg)\n\nSince $e^{-8t} \\to 0$ as $t \\to \\infty,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t \\to \\infty,$ so the origin is a stable node.\n\nThe phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/4c/4c337f7f6b80f340859844e8217525db98230660d22e760c70218f0c282d21e9.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "371d99ed-a060-51da-8f0f-7b38a0267bb7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fdba132-c503-57ae-93e5-9c8830e04d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b3/b32b5666c0138f5c17ff1622cef9bca6fb019375f6748b6422c11a547cfad282.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164328} {:answer/id #uuid "d04eb00b-beb1-5c65-9760-d3b1e42c9203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7e48266d30ae7c204b25e6eddca968d1b4ce9cd8e1c7b19cd20247fa66070f0b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164329} {:answer/id #uuid "10b40ea3-068d-5f03-a06f-88cfef36edfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/af95a94fa9c3bd233a679a30c0acede51ba03d1e52244b172974279d4ce5dbff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164330} {:answer/id #uuid "5a232d0a-9f37-5edc-9f3a-5dce4d291ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52f6032c8aa3fd791b80fec42ffb46941408e871435a208573441deb087dffdf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164331} {:answer/id #uuid "605c5bb6-423a-5a92-a612-e7a2d212ce9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eba955015a4b919c65dc24facb0baa6e745df134feac32feeae07c99d40ff4ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52f6032c8aa3fd791b80fec42ffb46941408e871435a208573441deb087dffdf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164331} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7f9cbd-030b-5df6-bd6a-059b832231b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164327}] :question/id #uuid "cb42e4f6-9c82-5ae7-9fb2-860a5f0fb548" :question/math-academy-id "q-332570" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=-2$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\nthat represents the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince ${e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/52/52f6032c8aa3fd791b80fec42ffb46941408e871435a208573441deb087dffdf.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83780e2d-f983-56a0-910d-4315acbd104a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2a/2acd3b0de16138b460a332cf6e4841e6caeeb5dbb23eef8f411dbdb5ce48ea42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164486} {:answer/id #uuid "85c55197-972e-5ae8-adc5-35de8dcbd9a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7e48266d30ae7c204b25e6eddca968d1b4ce9cd8e1c7b19cd20247fa66070f0b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164487} {:answer/id #uuid "aed621ee-dc79-51f3-b217-0d285b403ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/ea7ff4f032bade692953813c58b34ba62ab9c525c71ac13a2256dda6285e6620.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164488} {:answer/id #uuid "b77e3e0a-5eb0-5077-bf3d-98a59c2ef736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7b/7be65c63a4e5dcbe73fbc63faf3f061476ecd478cef8d58776bb843bfe84df2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164489} {:answer/id #uuid "6b10b504-d34f-55f9-9884-1fbd9169b090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eba955015a4b919c65dc24facb0baa6e745df134feac32feeae07c99d40ff4ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2a/2acd3b0de16138b460a332cf6e4841e6caeeb5dbb23eef8f411dbdb5ce48ea42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164486} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5300bb-a569-52b1-b06c-9159f68b1f49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164485}] :question/id #uuid "a2b2a037-2ba8-540a-a005-ca472e5f4072" :question/math-academy-id "q-333267" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=5$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{5t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{5t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={e}^{5t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{5t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince ${e}^{5t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/2a/2acd3b0de16138b460a332cf6e4841e6caeeb5dbb23eef8f411dbdb5ce48ea42.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05091666-67ba-551c-b9f1-c3ee8b2d8246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/87/87dfef6eaac680d1730a6b5537ecab4e5d1abee35dd58abf80c72c3afa01107b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305197} {:answer/id #uuid "35a31eb6-922e-5f1c-aa3e-46856846b11d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/904ec8bfe5c8f1b9a63becd782c82da68ef2a70894368418c3710d09bc029db1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305665} {:answer/id #uuid "b7a96595-9e8d-5646-bfe7-092058fb51f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6bdaece2579041f23a73323c4317751dfd8266364633bd2af258437b53d4a6f9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306865} {:answer/id #uuid "c30f08fa-f2db-5f11-8d03-086b6d17e6e4" :answer/type {:db/id