gin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince ${e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/90/904ec8bfe5c8f1b9a63becd782c82da68ef2a70894368418c3710d09bc029db1.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "252d0ad7-d5cd-50c4-be35-c39d84a2074f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/54eba0116ac434bdadbc878e8bd173b6174a42642cfcfe6825a8bdb178a3282c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305503} {:answer/id #uuid "47ff4d81-6159-58fe-ab71-0977f0a1f271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305850} {:answer/id #uuid "5f404f44-645e-5da0-aed3-54a4bf4b067c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7e48266d30ae7c204b25e6eddca968d1b4ce9cd8e1c7b19cd20247fa66070f0b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306067} {:answer/id #uuid "85b3957f-54ab-53ce-9eb4-cfd452c0cfbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ff/ff337e0120343c7c956afa5e49ea3b482fbd79fe363783a018842d1bfeb340d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306426} {:answer/id #uuid "f39f1ed3-32ea-5e33-a64c-eaa4cd449988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eba955015a4b919c65dc24facb0baa6e745df134feac32feeae07c99d40ff4ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305850} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddc63cbc-d503-5a89-9f7d-09df2d0d7e16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308220}] :question/id #uuid "3453e3b1-d01b-5d4c-b10e-7d0ad14fbf35" :question/math-academy-id "q-333274" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=6x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=6y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=6$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince ${e}^{6t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/40/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1f4977-7656-57c3-8cbb-1441f5da0862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eba955015a4b919c65dc24facb0baa6e745df134feac32feeae07c99d40ff4ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305420} {:answer/id #uuid "6a79fbed-5aca-5492-bdfe-b3e9acb4cf22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7e48266d30a