(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=3$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}={e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince ${e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/c4/c46568f3173dfeaab6e33e83269262e8692f13e245a42983ba1a9d4302ec5357.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391194 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2e15d48-bf85-5d42-ba3e-1338107759f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f975014051d49d3a3fbbba048c5def4ad4f6f0e88e65304fdb9bba6666b9a2a3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391196} {:answer/id #uuid "65ca2087-5574-543f-97e1-261c3be98f70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/44/440d53841ecc6606923528349393c30e201a125ca659de7f95a4749c5bdc58a9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391197} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd311f8-aa4b-592d-b8b0-22647607745a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a2/a27e83035006f198d454498aafe91624e0576ab43993bde970faf426a9e4cef2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391198} {:answer/id #uuid "8c888fa2-840a-5792-95ed-4a0909a9983c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.