ype {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336741} {:answer/id #uuid "d165dd0b-9b42-5b6a-9f6b-28e246987841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,4,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337867} {:answer/id #uuid "e7352ec2-7a0d-5ebf-a31d-d40e2d019fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,0,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338053} {:answer/id #uuid "f0909395-70c0-5762-9904-8d810196ed0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,4,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,4,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337867} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2b02092-894d-53b3-a075-231d42cd265a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338678}] :question/id #uuid "2f667cb4-f7f6-5e1d-984a-274c7afbeac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-71260" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3z &=0 \\\\ 4y+2z-1 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-2x+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-2,0,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $4y+2z-1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,4,2⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,3⟩\\times ⟨0,4,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-12i+4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-12,4,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086f5368-e828-52b2-91a9-64b0973c30d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-5,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336103} {:answer/id #uuid "1a55379d-1dd0-5770-a7d1-c7f2cb774197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336274} {:answer/id #uuid "21a0f372-608b-5fee-a050-b16d2e06eaf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨20,25,20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336345} {:answer/id #uuid "44ef7ab5-c764-5a1e-b178-38a24d78076f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,-4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336674} {:answer/id #uuid "497ed7bc-f539-55eb-b2d4-2434c210ae6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,-9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨20,25,20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336345} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b18175-4604-545f-86e0-7cd07ba8bb55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338477}] :question/id #uuid "f0178351-a186-5d55-9077-57136241af31" :question/math-academy-id "q-71266" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-4y &=0 \\\\ 4y-5z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-4y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨5,-4,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $4y-5z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,4,-5⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨5,-4,0⟩\\times ⟨0,4,-5⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =20i+25j+20k \\\\  & =⟨20,25,20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2ca58d-14d5-550f-920b-450010e3a59d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336424} {:answer/id #uuid "30e057c1-0768-5607-8a92-8c81c9a72911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336500} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d5c20f-bfcf-5ec2-ab0e-5c1c48e89403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337868} {:answer/id #uuid "e55f5c14-8d5d-5a4d-b6ad-6081f8abe5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338032} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7442f8-c86a-5193-9d60-4ee104cb74fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336424} :answer-field/id #uuid "90908b74-fc45-5e32-b466-62e0d10d8c44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338543}] :question/id #uuid "8dcce0be-d5f7-5cfa-b79c-7ffd73c0f53e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71269" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $x=1$ and $y=-z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $x=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y=-z$ (or $y+z=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d469811-ad49-51b7-ba98-f36dda7fa8bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,6,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388008} {:answer/id #uuid "55c95756-c3ad-51e7-bfd2-ff829b2645f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,-4,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388009} {:answer/id #uuid "7db145f2-bd3e-56ff-83a7-ec3ad48ffafe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,6,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388010} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ecd231-43e4-5db5-9f1d-b84553a750df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-6,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388011} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7b4075-2dcb-5db3-95e3-edb197f4913a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,6,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388010} :answer-field/id #uuid "38007ff1-e837-5245-a985-db1b0cc61194" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388007}] :question/id #uuid "d0aedac8-4550-5f55-b4ac-09ba9ac8ed13" :question/math-academy-id "q-129169" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3z-11 &=0 \\\\ 2x-2y-5 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x+3z-11=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-2y-5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,3⟩\\times ⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+6j-4k \\\\  & =⟨6,6,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907f2c4f-a7e3-593c-bb46-4fc277b70d5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,0,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388015} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2a73d2-b934-58fd-8801-1cf079a8a792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,15,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388016} {:answer/id #uuid "be16c1e5-86fe-53f6-b99a-b5cf526b20f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15,4,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388017} {:answer/id #uuid "c422581d-9fb0-51ca-8752-a801273ce3a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,6,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388018} {:answer/id #uuid "e459a854-7a51-5fab-8a48-995a7c6acd9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨14,11,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,15,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388016} :answer-field/id #uuid "1307634c-0843-58dc-9882-c76fe53c9f6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388014}] :question/id #uuid "85fcd4d1-25d1-559e-b810-7404c2aacc48" :question/math-academy-id "q-129171" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-2z+13 &=0 \\\\ 2y-3z-25 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-2z+13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨5,0,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2y-3z-25=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨5,0,-2⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+15j+10k \\\\  & =⟨4,15,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9137657-ea64-55ac-a50c-776389fe269a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388022} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb2d8a9-4b43-5c1d-a4f4-5266329e7446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388023} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb29629-4b1b-5406-ae1b-3f10adcfde85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388024} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5bcfcc-b800-5ca5-aba0-22a1220a9fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388025} {:answer/id #uuid "9b00eaee-d865-5c36-ba00-8bc6c7e12db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388024} :answer-field/id #uuid "8224c570-9b5e-580f-8450-ee7ed8cf16e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388021}] :question/id #uuid "c61ebc2f-8bbc-5c89-bcf3-6676fa54cd9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129174" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $2x=6$ and $z=1-y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $2x=6$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=1-y$ (or $y+z=1$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc33413-8200-5afe-93e6-6458c7c8e9bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393121} {:answer/id #uuid "a249b7e6-f321-572b-95e1-9881de3b676d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393122} {:answer/id #uuid "7a095b8f-ee85-53aa-bcff-2bfe68c67e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393123} {:answer/id #uuid "02a083d9-ebb3-54c7-86b9-863f7bd3eb31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393124} {:answer/id #uuid "0401bdc3-5a0a-5673-95e9-ba3ea18f4008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393123} :answer-field/id #uuid "faddb070-9799-589d-b442-8793b0a574ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393120}] :question/id #uuid "ce5171f6-22a8-5be0-9547-0d96404368c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71268" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $z=1$ and $x=y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $z=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=y$ (or $x-y=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa0ac3f8-438f-54c7-b4f9-c594d79dd1ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393128} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9dfc58-5aea-568f-92c8-b3bb1b22b61f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393129} {:answer/id #uuid "cd752dc0-22e1-56c0-97bc-d5c3b6653ad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393130} {:answer/id #uuid "a270c1dd-469b-558e-bafe-8ab31f4627af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393131} {:answer/id #uuid "a3354cd6-67f4-5aec-82d5-d960556c9346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393129} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dbac2a6-bbc5-5083-88c8-9b304da962d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393127}] :question/id #uuid "07f0b1a9-ab3f-550e-aed9-fa24adcc5d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-71270" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $y=-2$ and $x=z-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $y=-2$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=z-1$ (or $x-z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Direction Vector of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147343 :question/id #uuid "ae2be3b1-50fb-5abe-9f18-002a88f1de61" :question/math-academy-id "e-5921" :question/problem "Given the two planes $4x-2y=0$ and $-2x+y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nII. The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nIII. The planes intersect on a straight line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $4x-2y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_1 = \\langle 4,-2,0 \\rangle.$\n\n- For the plane $-2x+y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_2 = \\langle -2,1,0 \\rangle.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨4,-2,0⟩\\times ⟨-2,1,0⟩ \\\\ n & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\mathbf{n}_1 \\times \\mathbf{n}_2 =\\mathbf{0}$, the vectors $\\mathbf{n}_1$ and $\\mathbf{n}_2$ are parallel. However,  the first plane passes through the origin  $O(0,0,0)$ but the second plane doesn't: \n\n$$\n-2(0)+(0)+1=1 \\neq 0\n$$\n\n So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the planes are parallel but not coincident, they cannot intersect each other.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e6f4d22-2c99-5542-928b-c3b59936dc5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448732} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c58bba-fadc-524a-a8cc-494b4f99f03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448732} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a296daa-ab96-5c4a-a1f8-b78ea1e385cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16084eea-535d-5acb-adce-4de2cf9e9675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448734} {:answer/id #uuid "0f60ff85-a36c-5de6-b1ed-084a5b496106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448734} :answer-field/id #uuid "29d97c3e-8aa9-51c8-a4d7-7e07197c935d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449407} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adc0e532-ce8f-5ce5-ad6d-bd6230d11a37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448736} {:answer/id #uuid "d0817e09-8e2c-5a3f-ab83-e7c67840909f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448737} :answer-field/id #uuid "c388eae4-2ad8-5c93-87d1-98e87cfacc3b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449408}] :question/id #uuid "ddee53f3-5b0d-5dc0-9b9e-825db292f3e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71110" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x-y+z=0$ and $x-z+4=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x-y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-1,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-z+4=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,-1,1⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,4,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76964585-4ef5-5615-9266-030108aa4050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448738} {:answer/id #uuid "c21a224c-af73-599e-b06e-f16d286e621d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448739} :answer-field/id #uuid "245e5d53-a754-5a7f-9862-cfcd5697a920" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449409} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ac0ce90-fda3-5c34-8f4b-512bb9f1c72d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448740} {:answer/id #uuid "88e141fa-49d4-5fbe-bd6d-efc79acd7670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448741} :answer-field/id #uuid "024f89ce-ddf6-5369-86d7-244f8640e246" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77bc00cc-e71f-5e80-99b0-f29b6976627f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448742} {:answer/id #uuid "0db0ebbf-41d8-5103-a9e7-215c6eb2e315" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448742} :answer-field/id #uuid "05e8471d-d2bd-558a-82bf-518e8b2848f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449411}] :question/id #uuid "c8314953-42cd-5ac5-902d-92a3c570bac9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71112" :question/problem "Given the two planes $-x-2y+z=0$ and $2x+4y-2z+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- **II.** The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $-x-2y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+4y-2z+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${n}_{2}=-2{n}_{1}.$ So, the normal vectors are parallel.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFor the two planes to coincide, the equation of one plane should be a scalar multiple of the other. However, if we try to manipulate the equation of the second plane to resemble the equation of the first plane, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-2z+1=0 \\\\ x+2y-z+\\frac{1}{2}=0 \\\\ -x-2y+z-\\frac{1}{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nClearly, this equation is not the same as the equation of the first plane. So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c4244bc-8ceb-5e33-8598-38ab925f8b4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448314} {:answer/id #uuid "a4baa4cb-1e55-5d20-9fad-2d8fefbf1372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448314} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8142b6d-b401-52da-b7e4-0f8f6f82bcce" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65643d53-a883-5f0e-b168-41516f263752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448316} {:answer/id #uuid "fe198cb5-4419-5f30-8103-df3f434b8f73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448316} :answer-field/id #uuid "90ca466e-5705-5201-b9a5-5dca1c9735d0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a09c6d3-9e07-5bfa-a9af-913b460366de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448318} {:answer/id #uuid "401bbb80-3136-505b-91b2-a79e6cdcbae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448319} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a49394-7282-584c-b4ee-30af011d8280" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449199}] :question/id #uuid "5d967e86-9fda-51c5-b084-5eaf2a90df28" :question/math-academy-id "q-129239" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-5y+z+1=0$ and $3x-z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-5y+z+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-5,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x-z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,0,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-5,1⟩\\times ⟨3,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i+5j+15k \\\\  & =⟨5,5,15⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff5f8263-677b-5643-9c09-fbb882cb5e5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448320} {:answer/id #uuid "7e00f930-9bc2-5a8f-b341-6b3bfb849414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448321} :answer-field/id #uuid "c870b39a-efa3-5b75-abf3-729e6c1bb66c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449200} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddbba897-a72e-574e-bb64-100d9be232c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448322} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6d0ded-ecca-50de-8256-302276a8c0c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448323} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d641374-fb2b-5515-9551-b1f94e91baca" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4626da49-16af-5f92-be8b-0ede6458b582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448324} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac4ea5-c3ac-52b8-b780-d761ee6ccd2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448324} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af67d6f-4108-5880-b4ff-5f30c21746cc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449202}] :question/id #uuid "48d9b691-f927-556a-a0f4-054f943d7dcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-129240" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x-y+2z=0$ and $9x-3y+6z+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- **II.** The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $9x-3y+6z+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨9,-3,6⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${n}_{2}=3{n}_{1}.$ So, the normal vectors are parallel.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFor the two planes to coincide, the equation of one plane should be a scalar multiple of the other. However, if we try to manipulate the equation of the second plane to resemble the equation of the first plane, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3y+6z+5=0 \\\\ 3x-y+2z+\\frac{5}{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nClearly, this equation is not the same as the equation of the first plane. So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3bf1a8d-9dfc-5a03-8a7a-a12552a416b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448326} {:answer/id #uuid "30b819cc-54c9-5241-bcb2-0afe25ea1cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448326} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9949ae3-b6d9-5ef1-8624-bc499988813e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f26368b7-3e6e-5297-9b4f-7695649ea137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448328} {:answer/id #uuid "d00fa2fb-b244-56ee-b0ac-1b84182ea9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448328} :answer-field/id #uuid "c385d683-72a4-5ea4-b2a1-efdb9c6df55d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b6f951-e1c6-5513-a35c-3fa485d07fab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448330} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5c44e0-de54-563d-a94e-0a2b9889f8e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448331} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c21207d-f238-50e0-bf4e-370792bcf5f4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449205}] :question/id #uuid "c9f9477f-0f39-55d8-91e7-cff41b6de7c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-129241" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-3y+2z=0$ and $x-2y+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n\n- **II.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7823cc1d-e72d-50f4-af52-e5710e6619a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} {:answer/id #uuid "057d0176-e1f4-520c-a143-aa4e8964f2f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdffdf7c-e7ca-5a79-9cff-9