s ${n}_{2}=⟨3,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\times ⟨3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+6j+13k \\\\  & =⟨4,6,13⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0007c9-b9d9-5073-9847-1328f8ba456f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448338} {:answer/id #uuid "c07d5de8-6189-5107-a5d0-b648d30f4e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448338} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c49eabf-4bf6-5c32-9685-79efc670c417" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449209} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14bb3934-f6ec-59cd-99ae-ebf070b84930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448340} {:answer/id #uuid "a7dc5079-c112-5095-af24-842397e211d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448341} :answer-field/id #uuid "55c3de56-e97c-5d08-8dd0-16889f5908a4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8a1855-4689-53bf-ad30-730d170807be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448342} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4d1237-b5dc-5cb5-86d5-1b7a288207c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448342} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd284aa-2269-52c0-a105-e2d1597fba9e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449211}] :question/id #uuid "df6925db-161f-5f40-8f9d-0f308e52b4c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129259" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-y+3z=0$ and $5x-2y+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨7,15,2⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x-2y+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\times ⟨5,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+15j+k \\\\  & =⟨6,15,1⟩\\ne ⟨7,15,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes cannot be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225965e7-ea8b-53cc-8c0e-59f84b35bad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448344} {:answer/id #uuid "44625f5b-937b-5938-b07c-f560e2643779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07dfd5a-6ecb-5608-b7c1-bea7db6ba11f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f406006b-6b33-5be7-af63-0ad0b245352f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} {:answer/id #uuid "f15dcac9-93bd-55b2-9f31-b7ee83d2ce65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b07353-6adf-5e95-9046-04d5131fb4b2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d244ee5-d55d-5d5d-a779-19cd20f8d3e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448348} {:answer/id #uuid "81250b54-fda0-5220-8698-e14b62c96958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f1dcfe-3ed7-5654-8b55-b7e27497c7e8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449214}] :question/id #uuid "999cfdc7-ea79-5a7b-bd15-dce6f8b9e282" :question/math-academy-id "q-129260" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x+y-2z=0$ and $2x+y+3z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨5,-13,1⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+y-2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+y+3z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,1,3⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩\\times ⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i-13j+k \\\\  & =⟨5,-13,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only I and III only are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265704 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9480da-b8d7-5635-acad-ba1da8240664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448350} {:answer/id #uuid "ac1933c0-bd2f-5aff-beae-cb8cda84293b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448350} :answer-field/id #uuid "f40e5e28-4f88-5130-b328-64606e612555" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449215} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b291afa3-882c-5323-96b3-be71495fa5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448352} {:answer/id #uuid "c25385b7-80d0-51da-88a9-662a5e5b2c33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448353} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a4987ef-c77c-5b41-994f-27c06e153327" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a59e55b-0aa1-51df-b3d5-69f5f25a9700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448354} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf7ba73-0774-51da-bccc-e7f1bc26d6dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448354} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c03d44-f207-5cb2-b332-ad7675261ad8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449217}] :question/id #uuid "d9644136-e70e-5412-95e4-ddf24de80c84" :question/math-academy-id "q-129261" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-y+2z=0$ and $5x+y-13=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨-3,12,6⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x+y-13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-1,2⟩\\times ⟨5,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i+10j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,10,6⟩\\ne ⟨-3,12,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08a9d9fb-59ba-5f9e-9ed4-0dd4dd47d776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451513} {:answer/id #uuid "3353c7cf-f540-50b8-b410-f9464bae62df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451513} :answer-field/id #uuid "105aa68e-efe5-5792-a05e-ab62905759d4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37b877f-2a3f-5fed-9ad8-fb2c168a8f61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451515} {:answer/id #uuid "5aebbcaf-2c44-5bbd-8d57-983ab8f1a5ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451516} :answer-field/id #uuid "76c3952f-a2e7-5826-84ff-a1d6a0428f2c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452605} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a50e1758-2a18-5eda-97ec-ee302f243927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451517} {:answer/id #uuid "624bf4db-24cc-5399-8313-772b1909a576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451517} :answer-field/id #uuid "31fa76a4-c8ce-5442-94a2-8831eb85b68a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452606}] :question/id #uuid "59fa73e3-7e11-58b8-85f9-3fcdbce086ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-71456" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-3y+z=0$ and $2x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,5,2⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+2j+5k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,5⟩\\ne ⟨1,5,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes cannot be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e2afd41-011d-50b7-bdd6-b2fe0e79319a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451519} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a8a6a1-4d09-5b9a-87bf-b8affe56cc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451519} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ff5205-ba68-5bf5-9b0a-caec3fa1d55c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4573706-4ddd-5c59-ae75-f76209f442b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451521} {:answer/id #uuid "8a64a65e-cbd5-5aa2-9fc1-b39766e3b1ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451521} :answer-field/id #uuid "a02ea405-f5ad-5f66-b8b5-c7c965e15944" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452608} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e1367f-c77e-5db8-87a9-df2724a72ab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451523} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf169b7-e727-58e0-a834-1eca473c044e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451524} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ecb6f3e-52a7-56a2-9a87-95a8d2a508e8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452609}] :question/id #uuid "894f2787-9676-52de-a718-3b82f8fd7a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71463" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x+3y+2z=0$ and $x-y-z=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,6,-5⟩.$\n\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y-z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,3,2⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+5j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-6⟩\\ne ⟨1,6,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef64022-0288-5e76-8bb0-1ca193d77eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451525} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfde92f-2266-5a57-a77b-9186eb8b35e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451526} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbec3c98-7285-563e-ab93-4e996e9fbaae" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64e99a15-12e3-5f98-8c02-7a61a29e41e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451527} {:answer/id #uuid "1afa0967-d19f-5ead-9712-05b4c3746b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451527} :answer-field/id #uuid "193f4082-ae02-52c1-a2e0-34b89151c4b4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6bda1b9-d22e-5990-a8f9-5869cb11938f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451529} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e169a5-4cbe-5477-b7e2-f3cb319f9ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451530} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b3bf2b-8f9f-51d2-b5f4-e6f63de89d4f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452612}] :question/id #uuid "55226586-d156-5c41-9a9d-ff9a0c5b3e34" :question/math-academy-id "q-71464" :question/problem "Given the two planes $y-z=1$ and $2x+z=3$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,-2,-2⟩.$\n- **II.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y-z=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,-1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+z=3,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,-1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and  III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338951 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96dfc723-c739-5f3e-8f21-0b626c09e1d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451531} {:answer/id #uuid "97b76965-dd4a-52ed-930f-e1d960bbf66b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74be5fe-bbae-51b8-be42-776a486c8913" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "819e2d79-747a-537e-b412-468c4ceadea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451533} {:answer/id #uuid "036ccda4-6962-5c5a-82b9-fcd5b6624f98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451533} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c2940e9-01bd-5899-9120-b872a698e75e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "564ac206-0781-50cf-81c9-0e7b9d70d384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451535} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ad7deb-c245-5226-b91a-5ea92b19e6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451535} :answer-field/id #uuid "9551997d-c399-5b54-b209-0e56d0ead71f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452615}] :question/id #uuid "eb6d9712-df0c-5f4b-a820-ccc73d9a1ec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71468" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-4y+6z+2=0$ and $-x+2y-3z=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a straight line.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-4y+6z+2=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-4,6⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $-x+2y-3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨-1,2,-3⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-4,6⟩\\times ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =0i+0j+0k \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}=0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes are also parallel. So, the planes can't intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed,  the second plane passes through the origin  $O(0,0,0)$ but the first plane doesn't: \n\n$$\n2(0)-4(0)+6(0)+2=2\\ne 0\n$$\n\n So, the planes can't be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfbaf102-c0df-5e93-9fdd-76ff8e170914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451507} {:answer/id #uuid "bd856043-9bf5-545a-9dab-355b675c30de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451507} :answer-field/id #uuid "17379ff6-7738-574d-b3f4-b367ff0dfb86" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eacdbb44-ca0c-548a-9e83-9c47d872f78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451509} {:answer/id #uuid "f26307df-edf9-5e2f-ae55-61a18a228540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451509} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1aea80c-069f-5199-b8cf-083b0c70f9f9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5d27925-4f17-57c7-83c0-083d924358a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451511} {:answer/id #uuid "b187a096-71e0-5c74-af3c-85207909140b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451512} :answer-field/id #uuid "22f7c0e5-f396-5066-adbe-dbe1244d165d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452603}] :question/id #uuid "96c9a429-d310-55eb-845b-95fc86ca78d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71448" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-2y+z=0$ and $x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- **II.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a139c706-0e77-54a4-accb-bfe443670e5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453922} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a0a00e-bd44-522f-87a0-1661c0717d26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453922} :answer-field/id #uuid "227c754c-4dc6-54d5-bd20-dc203c3bd56d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454711} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a8ed31-2bd6-5da1-bce7-520c67f0b586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453924} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef7da89-3321-5d51-9ea4-d7214de7dcff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453925} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d5956ce-b17c-56a5-9c55-441171fc7b01" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c079efb-b705-50e6-8fa4-f8d29cbaf064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453926} {:answer/id #uuid "313e94f5-659f-51cb-b0fd-10e36f25ce06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453926} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7ace9d-04e4-53a1-8f3e-3670bba92643" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454713}] :question/id #uuid "abe7bafd-4069-5c23-9e34-e0cbd57e3732" :question/math-academy-id "q-71465" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x+y+z=0$ and $x+y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,1,0⟩.$\n\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x+y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,1,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x+y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\times ⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+j \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩\\ne ⟨1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd4e332-b156-59b1-ae2a-6ee0a08db8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559042} {:answer/id #uuid "41b5d577-0fb3-59f4-8ba7-b4b1fb1a2178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559183} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd38e05-67b8-5a94-8742-6e3af398c4d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559414} {:answer/id #uuid "b421ec28-5bd3-59b4-af01-a5ba41d5c3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559467} {:answer/id #uuid "df0cddb8-e92c-55c7-aa50-0c028229c858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559042} :answer-field/id #uuid "2364b0d7-2e01-5066-ae19-026ea99bfd99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559660}] :question/id #uuid "e8cdac5c-1e47-510f-8a9c-c4df54b69f10" :question/math-academy-id "q-71467" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x-6y+1=0$ and $-x+2y=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n\nII. The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nIII. The planes intersect in a straight line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:  \n\n- For the plane $3x-6y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-6,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $-x+2y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨-1,2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,-6,0⟩\\times ⟨-1,2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =0i+0j+0k \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}=0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are parallel. However,  the second plane passes through the origin  $O(0,0,0)$ but the first plane doesn't: \n\n$$\n3(0)-6(0)+1=1\\ne 0\n$$\n\n So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since planes are parallel but not coincident, they cannot intersect.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}
